## 7. PRODUCT IMPORT workstream (user's immediate task)

**Goal:** 12 to 15 products first (6 almond sets, 6 coffin sets, 2 to 3 accessories) so both shape pages reach the 6-product indexing rule; then grow.

**Flow, one product at a time:**
1. **In the CJ app** (Product List → Add to Import List → Import to Store; button names may differ): choose only the variants you want to sell (the panel cannot add or remove variants), pick the warehouse and shipping method (**US warehouse ships to the US only; China warehouse ships worldwide**), skip any product whose images have watermarks, logos or foreign text. Do **not** bother editing titles, descriptions or prices at the CJ stage; the admin panel does it.
2. **Set the price with free shipping in mind.** Free shipping is on every order, so price = CJ product cost + shipping to the destination + payment fees + margin. Check CJ's shipping cost to US, UK, Canada, Australia for each product. The panel only checks that a price exists, not that it makes money. Use a compare-at ("was") price **only if it is a real previous price** (fake crossed-out prices are a legal risk).
3. **Check the imported product's status in Shopify.** If it imports as Active it may already appear on the old `shop.mirelleinspo.com` storefront with CJ's raw text. Set unfinished products to **Draft** until finished.
4. **Finish it in `/admin/store`:** open it by link, rewrite the description in the user's own words (suggested 30+ words), write alt text for each image, remove junk images, choose the main image, click category buttons (**always `Type: Press-On Set` for nail sets**, plus shape, length, style, finish, color, occasion), set the SEO title (<= 60 characters) and meta (<= 155) or leave empty for the automatic ones, tick **Show on the store**, **Save & publish**.
5. **Bulk path for 10+ products:** import all first; in the list tick all sets and add `Type: Press-On Set`; tick all almond ones and add `Shape: Almond`; repeat for length and style; tick all and **Publish to store**; then open each only to rewrite description and alt text.
6. After publishing a batch, click **Update sitemap**.
7. Make sure **only nail products** (plus accessories) are published to the Headless channel. The old winter coat product is on the old channel for the vintage ad; if it is published to Headless it appears in `/store/collections/all` and "New arrivals".

