- **Never** use fake countdown timers, "only 3 left" counters that are not real stock, invented "12 people viewing now", made-up reviews/testimonials/ratings, or fake "was" prices. I believe the UK has restricted fake urgency and fake reviews since April 2025 and the US FTC has a rule against fake reviews; **verify**. A permanent 15% code is not a "sale": do not show crossed-out invented original prices next to it.
- Fine and encouraged: bold color and large type, real coupons with the conditions shown, progress bars toward real thresholds, bundles, sticky add-to-cart, real social proof from real data, microinteractions, product-benefit icons, clear delivery and returns messaging that matches `policy.ts`.
- All shipping/returns claims must come from `policy.ts`; do not hard-code numbers in components.

